{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## HANDOFF-3B5F: implementation delegated to a subagent; plan is attested, do not redesign it\n\nState: `in_progress`, claimed. Plan-review verdict **PASS, signed**. A subagent is implementing steps\nA0/A/B/B1/C/D/E from the description. No code had been written at handoff time.\n\n**The decision is settled — read DECISION-3B5F-C before touching anything.** It is *re-home*, not the\nwire-or-delete the brief offered:\n\n* the deletion discrimination is already live twice (`outbound_differ._safe_get_issue`,\n  `binding_walk.py:187-196`), verified on real DC (Row 14 PASSED, run 30933704255);\n* prior art rejects resurrection — Unito will not re-create deleted work items, deliberately; Kubernetes\n  reconcilers `IgnoreNotFound` and never resurrect;\n* so under the operator's ruling (\"once deleted in Jira, never resurrected\") the resurrection\n  IMPLEMENTATION is removed rather than orphaned, AND a tombstone guard stops the EXISTING\n  eventual-resurrection path.\n\n**Measured, so it does not need re-deriving:** 3 consecutive confirmed-404 `note_absent` calls retire the\nbinding; `_retire` (`binding_store.py:564-577`) pops it from BOTH `bindings` and `reverse`;\n`get_jira_key` then returns `None`; and `outbound_differ.py:502-513` creates a fresh Jira issue for any\nunbound local ticket. That is the resurrection to stop.\n\n**Three traps, each already cost someone something:**\n1. `drop_snapshot_differ_local_state_emissions` STAYS — the caller is unchanged, so it remains correct.\n   The ticket's \"what is NOT the fix\" warning is about the WIRE option, which is not being taken.\n2. The port capability (`probe_remote`, `SupportsAbsenceProbe`, `inbound_probe.py`) STAYS — removing\n   DC's `probe_remote` drops DC's only import of the shared `classify_probe_response`, leaving it\n   Cloud-only and weakening epic e369's AC5. Reasoned exclusion, recorded as plan step B1.\n3. Engine modules load BY FILENAME STRING through a dynamic loader. For every symbol removed, ALSO grep\n   the name as a string — an import-graph check alone misses the call site.\n\nVerify the subagent's work against the ACs before closing; do not close on its report alone."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785878519226132001,"uuid":"cd97ba45-4eae-4ae2-8763-b07077ca9fb9"}